  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "For decades, gold followed one simple rule. Now it's breaking that rule, doing something it historically should not.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "fire"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "Gold broke",
            "the rule."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The old rule, when real interest rates rise, gold usually falls, because cash suddenly pays you to hold it.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "truth",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "kicker": "the old rule",
          "line": "High rates, low gold",
          "sub": "they normally move opposite"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The real interest rate is the return on cash after inflation.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-realrate",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · real interest rate"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Lately, real rates rose, and yet gold climbed to record highs anyway. The link snapped.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "big": "both up",
          "label": "rates AND gold — unusual",
          "props": [
            "chartUp",
            "fire"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So who is buying so hard that they override the old math? Increasingly, it's central banks.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Central banks buying",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "globe"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Central banks hold gold reserves as a backstop outside any one currency.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-goldres",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · gold reserve"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "They're quietly swapping dollars for gold, hedging against the dollar system itself.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "center",
